INV-fazim's consumer clause. `_match_propagation_entry`'s is_resolved arm
compares a catalogue entry's declared module against the dst symbol's own path.
When the dst carried no path evidence -- external-shaped, or malformed enough
that `_extract_callee_module` returns falsy -- it fell through to
`return hits[0]`: an ungated bare-name match with no receiver verification at
all. That is the same escape WI-damir measured 30 of 30 FALSE on a nine-repo
cohort (caddy's `func Log()` as a logging sink 18 times; d3's `log()`, the
LOGARITHM, as console.log), reached through a different door -- not by being a
first-party symbol, but by being flagged resolved while carrying nothing to
verify. ADR-0037 ruling 4 makes the flag authoritative, so a producer that set
it wrongly landed straight here. It now refuses.

THE LICENCE IS A MEASUREMENT, AND THE ITEM REQUIRED A NON-TAUTOLOGICAL ONE.
Both obvious measurements are tautologies: finalize's edge-resolution sub-step
sets is_resolved=True IFF the dst is an in-repo node -- whose path slot is a
real path -- so counting "edges resolved at an external path slot" returns zero
whether or not the branch is reachable. It measures finalize's definition, not
the branch. The thread warned twice against filing a third such zero.

So the branch was OBSERVED during real verify-claims runs, recording
production's own inputs and classifying them with production's own
`_module_from_symbol_path`:

    repo      calls    is_resolved=True    escape condition
    sops       7,738            2,592            0
    grype     25,178            9,380            0
    act       10,696            3,222            0
    poetry    24,660            9,666            0
    winston    1,936            1,190            0
    knex      28,214           22,466            0
    TOTAL     98,422           48,516            0

Five languages. The counted condition is a SUPERSET of the branch (it ignores
the non-empty `hits` requirement), so it errs toward over-reporting. A positive
control driving the branch deliberately fires it, so the zero is a property of
the inputs and not of a probe that never attached.

That is what licenses the change, because this index also backs SANITIZER
registration: losing a sanitizer match loses a barrier, which moves flows the
opposite way from losing a sink. A line that never executes can do neither.

86 FIXTURES WERE THE ESCAPE'S ONLY CONSUMERS. Correcting the branch reddened 22
tests, none a real regression: their edge dicts pair an external-shaped dst with
NO is_resolved key, so they took the resolved arm through
`edge.get('is_resolved', True)` -- a fail-open default. Declaring
is_resolved=False, which is what production stamps for an external dst
post-finalize, restores every assertion and routes them through
`_lookup_named_entry`, the arm that owns unresolved callees along with the F3
untyped-method gate.

The 2026-08-17 note asked for that default to be "confirmed against the finalize
stage before the consumer gate is designed". Confirmed, and it is DEAD in
production: all 158,116 edges of a full self-survey carry is_resolved explicitly
(114,456 true / 43,660 false), none omit it. The default was reachable only from
hand-built fixtures.

THE SWEEP'S OWN FIRST PASS HAD THE BLIND SPOT ITS PLAYBOOK NAMES. An AST pass
over edge-dict literals corrected 83 and left 12 red -- all reached through
helpers building the dst with an f-string, which matches no literal and which
the fundamental-concept audit lists as producer-emit shape 4, "literal-substring
grep misses these entirely". Ten of the twelve were in the sanitizer suite, the
direction this item warns about by name. They were fixture declarations, not
lost barriers: annotating the two helpers restored all twelve.

AND THE FINDINGS A/B WAS RUN ANYWAY, because the item asks for it in those
terms rather than for an entailment. Arms differ only in the one hunk; per-arm
XDG_CACHE_HOME so neither can read the other's behaviour map; sops / poetry /
winston against the six generic taint claims:

    TOTAL findings  A=52  B=52  delta=0

Every verdict and every count identical, including violated/14, violated/19 and
violated/6 — so this is not a zero-against-zero comparison. Arm A asserted the
escape was actually back before measuring.

